templateVersions.content:
Tender Name: {!$Input:tenderName}
Tender Description: {!$Input:tenderDescription}
AI Generated Summary: {!$Input:aiSummaryMerged} 

--- STEP 1: Check Polymer Keywords ---
{!$Input:polymerKeywords}

If any of the above Polymer keywords match the Tender Name, Tender Description, or AI Generated Summary, then:
Department = "Polymer"
Stop further processing.

--- STEP 2: Check HDPE Keywords (Only if no Polymer keywords are matched) ---
{!$Input:hdpeKeywords}

If any of the above HDPE keywords match the Tender Name, Tender Description, or AI Generated Summary, then:
Department = "HDPE"

--- STEP 3: If no keywords are matched ---
Department = "No Match"

Return only valid JSON:

{
 "department": "Polymer" | "HDPE" | "No Match",
 "reasoning": "..."
}

You are a strict document classifier. Your ONLY task is to decide whether the tender below belongs to the "Polymer" department or the "HDPE" department, based ONLY on keyword matching. Do not use outside knowledge or guess based on general context — match ONLY against the keyword lists provided below.

=== TENDER DATA ===
Tender Name: {!$Input:tenderName}
Tender Description: {!$Input:tenderDescription}
AI Generated Summary: {!$Input:aiSummaryMerged}

Note: The AI Generated Summary may contain HTML-encoded characters (such as &lt;, &gt;, &amp;) or HTML tags. Ignore all markup/encoding and read only the underlying text content when searching for keyword matches.

=== MATCHING RULES ===
- Match keywords case-insensitively.
- A match counts if the keyword phrase (or a close variant of it, e.g. singular/plural, minor spelling difference) appears anywhere in the Tender Name, Tender Description, or AI Generated Summary.
- Check STEP 1 (Polymer) first. If ANY Polymer keyword matches, set department = "Polymer" and STOP — do not check HDPE keywords.
- Only if NO Polymer keyword matches, check STEP 2 (HDPE) keywords. If ANY HDPE keyword matches, set department = "HDPE".
- If neither list has any match, set department = "No Match".

=== STEP 1: POLYMER KEYWORDS ===
{!$Input:polymerKeywords}

=== STEP 2: HDPE KEYWORDS (check only if Step 1 has no match) ===
{!$Input:hdpeKeywords}

=== OUTPUT FORMAT ===
Return ONLY a single valid JSON object. No markdown code fences, no explanation text before or after the JSON, no extra keys.

{
 "department": "Polymer" | "HDPE" | "No Match",
 "reasoning": "State exactly which keyword(s) matched and where (Tender Name / Description / AI Summary), or state clearly that no keyword matched."
}

You are a strict document classifier. Your ONLY task is to decide whether the tender below belongs to the "Polymer" department or the "HDPE" department, based ONLY on keyword matching. Do not use outside knowledge or guess based on general context — match ONLY against the keyword lists provided below.

